<title>JAMAICA: SOCCER-JAMAICA BEAT ST VINCENT 5-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-JAMAICA BEAT ST VINCENT 5-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>KINGSTON 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jamaica beat St Vincent 5-0</p>
<p>(halftime 2-0) in a CONCACAF semifinal stage group three World</p>
<p>Cup qualifying match on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Theodore Whitmore (10th and 13th minutes), Paul</p>
<p>Young (64th), Peter Cargil (66th), Onandi Lowe (85th).</p>
<p>Attendance: 20,000</p>
<p>Group three standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn,</p>
<p>lost, goals for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Mexico	  5  4  0  1 15  5 12</p>
<p> Jamaica	 5  3  1  1 12  3 10</p>
<p> Honduras	5  2  1  2  7  8  7</p>
<p> St Vincent    4  0  0  4  3 21  0</p>
<p>Next matches: Nov 17 - Jamaica v Mexico, Honduras v St</p>
<p>Vincent.</p>
<p>Top two teams qualify for the final CONCACAF qualifying</p>
<p>round.</p>
</text>
